<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Travel</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Spell Tier: 4
Class: Sorcerer (guild level 150)
Mana: 60
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast travel &lt;someone or something&gt;
enter gate
untie        (close your gate)
</pre>
<p>Possibly the most powerful spell in the world: the caster clears their 
mind, focuses on the flame within, and cuts a hole through space to the 
person or thing named, anywhere in the world. A gate opens beside you and 
another at the far end. Unlike a portal (see <a cmd='#'>Help Portal</a>), a travel 
gate isn't used up: anyone can step through it, either way, as often as 
they like, for as long as it lasts. Look in it first to glimpse the far 
side.
</p><p>The gates last for some minutes, longer the better your magic, brain and 
skill in the spell, unless you close them sooner by typing untie. You can 
keep only one gate at a time: cast travel again, and your first gate 
closes.
</p><p>A master of the spell (skill 100) can deny others the use of the gate, and 
grant it again (grant, or grant group for your followers only), at 10 mana 
each.
</p><p>The far end resists: a player's own skill in the spell, a monster's in 
summoning, makes it harder to reach them. A poor casting does nothing; a 
very bad one opens a rift that sweeps you away. Some places can't be 
reached. You must be standing. It is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
